  "author_notes": "Written only from sources/biology-bs.md. Grades default A (letter). Pass records start fall 2026 so CHEM 3B/3C need no separate labs, except the transfer trap which took them in 2025 with CHEM 3BL/3CL. Avoided: the STAT 5 waiver (needs advisor contact), the BIOL 20L community-college exemption (stated only in transfer admission), the at-least-half-UD-at-UCSC rule (all UD in records is at UCSC), whether a 2-credit BIOE lab (e.g. BIOE 117L) alone can be the additional L course, whether a first-list lab like METX 100L can double as the additional lab, and whether the additional lab may also count as one of the two BIOE DC courses (pass records avoid depending on it). The MATH 19A->MATH 11B transition in the trap case relies on the note permitting transitions between the 11 and 19 series; the external Calculus Series Transition Policy is not part of the source. AUDIT: removed fail-mixed-math16a-math11b as ambiguous: the page defers series mixing to the external Calculus Series Transition Policy, whose content is not in the source, so whether MATH 16A -> MATH 11B is allowed cannot be settled from the page.",
